The page body is now stored in the `main` region of `blocks`, with `"@type": "plate"`, instead of the `__somersault__` block. Content with the old block is renamed when it is read, through the new `contentMigration` utility type, and keeps the new shape once it is saved. The backend must index and process `plate` regions (plone.restapi, or `volto-plate` for its own handlers) before deploying this version. @sneridagh
